WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.740
Moses Maimonides, who
lived from 1138 to 1204,

2
00:00:04.790 --> 00:00:08.900
drew up a list: 13
principles of Jewish faith.

3
00:00:08.950 --> 00:00:12.880
Many Jews still sing them
today, in a hymn called Yigdal.

4
00:00:12.930 --> 00:00:15.840
Yet Judaism's best-known words are a call,

5
00:00:15.890 --> 00:00:18.890
not a proof: Hear, O Israel.

6
00:00:18.940 --> 00:00:21.790
So does a Jew have to
believe things about God,

7
00:00:21.840 --> 00:00:25.010
or mainly trust God and
keep the commandments?

8
00:00:25.060 --> 00:00:28.890
In this mission, you'll meet Jewish
thinkers who argued with philosophy for over

9
00:00:28.940 --> 00:00:30.550
a thousand years.

10
00:00:30.600 --> 00:00:34.680
Then you'll ask how belief in a
just God has faced the Holocaust.

11
00:00:34.730 --> 00:00:39.110
Your mission: weigh up whether
Judaism asks Jews mainly to believe,

12
00:00:39.160 --> 00:00:40.830
to trust, or both.
